 "story": "Rates are doing the talking. The 10-yr Treasury climbed to 5.24% (+106 bp YTD) and the 30-yr mortgage rate crossed 7% (7.03%) in the two weeks after the Fed's Sep 16 hike, and the S&P 500 slipped to +12.1% YTD. The labor data stayed firm at the front end \u2014 initial claims fell to 197K, beating the 201K consensus \u2014 but demand for workers cooled: JOLTS openings dropped to 7,079K against 7,225K expected. Housing sent mixed signals: new home sales jumped 6.4% to 684K, far above the 618K consensus, and pending sales edged up 0.3%, while final September sentiment slipped to a four-month low of 48.1 with year-ahead inflation expectations at 4.6%. Durable goods orders were flat, a touch better than the \u22120.3% expected.",
